{"title":"Obtuse angle","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>An <b>obtuse angle</b> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angle</a> with a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Measure\" title=\"Measure\">measure</a> greater than 90 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Degree_(geometry)\" title=\"Degree (geometry)\"> degrees</a> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/2/1b28eb5c39d0df30d06036f3cf179a5ddeff4d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac\\pi2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radian\" title=\"Radian\">radians</a>) but less than 180 degrees (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> radians).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"In_triangles\">In triangles</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Obtuse_angle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: In triangles\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Any triangle with an obtuse angle is considered an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Obtuse_Triangle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Obtuse Triangle\">Obtuse Triangle</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Obtuse_angle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">Geometry</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Obtuse_triangle\" title=\"Obtuse triangle\">Obtuse triangle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">Angle</a>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_angle\" title=\"Right angle\">Right angle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Acute_angle\" title=\"Acute angle\">Acute angle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Straight_angle\" title=\"Straight angle\">Straight angle</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Reflex_angle\" title=\"Reflex angle\">Reflex angle</a></li></ul></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Obtuse_angle&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003004\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 27/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 277/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 324/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.253      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.253      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4016:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003004 and revision id 228517. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}